WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.072 --> 00:00:05.813
I'm Kevin Tran, Chief Information Security
Officer at Kestrel Falls Community

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:06.413
Hospital.

3
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:07.555
My memo is in your files.

4
00:00:07.555 --> 00:00:08.909
Here's the short version.

5
00:00:08.909 --> 00:00:13.094
The move to a new EHR is the most
dangerous time for a cyberattack.

6
00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:14.760
Five risks worry me.

7
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.360
One.

8
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.575
Shared administrator logins.

9
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:21.398
Plexmoor still has twelve administrator
accounts shared by several people.

10
00:00:21.398 --> 00:00:24.907
If one is misused, we can't
tell who did it.

11
00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:25.507
Two.

12
00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:26.638
Vendor remote access.

13
00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:30.509
About one hundred forty vendor and contractor
accounts can reach our network,

14
00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.520
up from one hundred eighteen in October.

15
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:39.238
The new vendor will add more, and we have no
single list of who can reach what.

16
00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.586
Three.

17
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:41.186
Phishing.

18
00:00:41.051 --> 00:00:45.023
In our January test, nine percent of
staff clicked the fake link.

19
00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:50.173
Attackers like big changes, when people expect
strange emails about new logins.

20
00:00:50.173 --> 00:00:51.467
Four.

21
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.067
Data in motion.

22
00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:56.633
During migration, copies of patient
records sit in test systems,

23
00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:58.473
and test systems usually have
weaker protection.

24
00:00:58.473 --> 00:00:59.073
Five.

25
00:00:58.473 --> 00:01:00.082
Ransomware.

26
00:01:00.082 --> 00:01:04.805
If someone locks our systems near go-live, we
could be on paper for days or weeks.

27
00:01:04.805 --> 00:01:06.705
We last practiced our downtime
procedures in 2025.

28
00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:11.828
For scale, IBM's 2025 Cost of a Data Breach
report puts the average healthcare

29
00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:14.746
breach at seven point four two
million dollars.

30
00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:17.832
What I need: a named account for
every administrator,

31
00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:21.717
monthly vendor access reviews, phishing
training timed to go-live,

32
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:26.163
test systems protected like the real one, and
a downtime drill before go-live.

33
00:01:26.163 --> 00:01:27.657
I support this project.

34
00:01:27.657 --> 00:01:30.840
I just want us to get there
without a breach.

